# the astronomy tool gcx in Debian 12 and Ubuntu 22.04 installs /usr/bin/gcx too
Conflicts: gcx
Description: command-line tool for Grafana and Grafana Cloud
 gcx manages Grafana and Grafana Cloud resources from the command line:
 dashboards, datasources, alerting, and the Cloud product APIs such as SLO,
 IRM, Synthetic Monitoring, Fleet and k6. It is designed to be driven by AI
 agents as well as by people.
 .
 This package turns off the anonymous usage telemetry by default (opt in with
 GCX_TELEMETRY=enabled or `diagnostics.telemetry: enabled` in the gcx config)
 and the check for new gcx releases on GitHub; updates come through the package
 manager.
